  "what_this_establishes": "that the picture the page draws is displaced from the publication it draws, by up to 0.37 of a row, and how many structures stand where that displacement puts a colour that contradicts their own card",
  "what_this_does_not_establish": "that MapLibre places the quad this way. The rule is read off the canvas-source contract and matches the one behind the published 131,571 figure, and no browser had confirmed it when this was written. One did on 2026-11-15 -- eleven probes, zero disagreements, s3-11-browser-placement.json. The `probes` section is that session's oracle, and the sensitive probes are the ones that can fail. It also says nothing about the source grid: that step is s3-5-export-regrid.json, and pass 54's point is that folding the two together would hand a correct measurement the wrong interpretation. And one further step is left out on purpose: the raster is drawn at SCREEN resolution with nearest resampling, so which texel a screen pixel takes depends on the zoom -- at the opening fit the footprint is about 620 pixels tall for 514 rows, so a screen pixel spans more than a row and adds a quantisation of its own. The figures here are the zoom-independent part: the colour the placement assigns at a structure's exact latitude. Rolling the zoom in would be the same conflation in a smaller form"
